# The .vtu/.vtp test fixtures carry inline base64 payloads and are generated
# files (tests/fixtures/_gen_fixtures.py), so git must leave their bytes exactly
# as written. With core.autocrlf=true -- the Windows default, and what this repo
# is developed on -- git would otherwise store LF and check out CRLF: the file on
# disk would differ from what the generator produces, every regeneration would
# show spurious diffs, and the bytes under test would not be the same on Windows
# as on the Linux CI runner.
#
# Deliberately not applied to the .vtk/.vertex fixtures, which are ASCII and have
# been read correctly under CRLF conversion since they were added. Marking them
# now would only force a renormalization for no gain.
tests/fixtures/**/*.vtu -text
tests/fixtures/**/*.vtp -text
